## Review checklist

- [ ] I reviewed the advisory summary, severities, CVE counts, and affected package counts.
- [ ] I reviewed the visible finding sample and understand the complete advisory ID set is preserved in hidden scanner metadata for drift protection.
- [ ] I understand the update workflow will re-scan first and refuse to continue if the OpenSCAP advisory set drifted.
- [ ] I understand the update workflow reports Ksplice availability but only applies approved advisories through DNF's advisory-scoped update path.

## One-click approval

Apply the label `{{ security_patching_approval_label }}` to this issue to run the production security update workflow.

Only users listed in `.github/production-patch-approvers.yml` are allowed to approve production updates. The workflow removes the approval label after it starts and closes this issue only if the post-update scan is clean.
